graph TD
    subgraph "Algorithms = Everyday Search Strategies"
        direction TB
        LINEAR_SEARCH["ROLL CALL SEARCH
= Linear Search O(n)
Ask every person ONE BY ONE
'Does anyone have my keys?'
Guaranteed to find an answer
But SLOW for 1000 people"]
        
        BINARY_SEARCH["DICTIONARY SEARCH
= Binary Search O(log n)
'Is the word in the first half? No.'
'In the next quarter? Yes.'
'In the next eighth? Yes.'
Direct to specific section
FAST but requires sorted data"]
        
        GREEDY["SNACK CHOICE
= Greedy Algorithm
'What's the best option RIGHT NOW?'
Make the immediate best choice
May miss the long-term best option
Fast but not always optimal"]
        
        DIVIDE_CONQUER["SORTING A DECK
= Divide & Conquer
Split the deck into smaller piles
Sort each pile separately
Combine the sorted piles
'Break a big task into parts,
   finish each, then combine'"]
    end
    
    KEY["The RIGHT algorithm
depends on your data
and your constraints.
Knowing WHEN to use which
strategy wins the day."]
    
    style LINEAR_SEARCH fill:#ffe6e6,stroke:#cc0000
    style BINARY_SEARCH fill:#e6ffe6,stroke:#00cc00
    style DIVIDE_CONQUER fill:#e6f3ff,stroke:#0066cc,stroke-width:2px
    style KEY fill:#ffffe6,stroke:#cccc00,stroke-width:2px
